# MC-X-F7. L §5.12 (a fill's output F[y].taken[...] is read like any keyed value) and §5.14.1 (a plan's amounts read
# facts and defs): the plan refund[y] reads f[y].taken in its leg's amount, and f's supply reads only the contribs
# movements, which refund is not one of, so nothing reads f inside its own supply. refcore checked moves before fills
# and took the early read for one; the fill is now checked where a move first reads it. Every contribs amount is 0, so
# the supply and each demand are 0.00 PLN and every take is 0.00 PLN. snap10 refused the load (REFCORE-NOT-YET fill f
# read inside its own supply ...).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2025-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind contribs: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place acct: claims PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2025-01-01..
fill f[y in years]
  supply sum(c.cash.amount for c in contribs over y)
  demand c.cash.amount for c in contribs over y
  arc true
  order c.day
move pay[m in months]: contribs
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to acct amount 0
move refund[y in years]: transfers
  on end_of(y)
  leg cash from acct to world amount sum(f[y].taken[c] for c in contribs over y)
ask t: f[2027].taken[c] for c in contribs over 2027
=== expect
t (c = pay[2027-01]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-02]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-03]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-04]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-05]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-06]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-07]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-08]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-09]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-10]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-11]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t (c = pay[2027-12]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
